; isort-idempotent.proof — insertion sort is IDEMPOTENT on sorted lists: forall l. sorted(l)=True -> isort(l)=l.
; Sorting an already-sorted list returns it unchanged (a fixed-point property). Helpers: insert-front-when-le
; (sorted(Cons h t) -> insert(t,h)=Cons h t, since h<=head t makes insert prepend) via and-true-left + the insert-
; reduce prepend lemma; sorted-tail. Induction on l: Cons h t -> isort(Cons h t)=insert(isort t, h) =[IH isort t=t]
; insert(t,h) =[insert-front-when-le] Cons h t.
